&lt;p&gt;Since 1961, the &lt;a href="https://folkartmuseum.org/"&gt;American Folk Art Museum&lt;/a&gt; has showcased the exceptional talents and creativity of artists who have refined their art through personal experience and innovative vision. As part of the &lt;strong&gt;Legacy of New York&lt;/strong&gt; series, you&amp;rsquo;re invited to join an excursion with University Life to the museum at Lincoln Square to witness &lt;a href="https://www.3arts.org/artist/alexandria-eregbu/"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alexandria Eregbu&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&amp;rsquo;s exhibition &lt;a href="https://folkartmuseum.org/programs/blue-magic-2-21-26/?ID=35359"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Blue Magic&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a sonic and textile experience exploring the deep histories of the color blue, Eregbu&amp;rsquo;s exhibition draws from American quilting practices, oral storytelling, sound, and her own family history as a Nigerian-American. Her work serves to honor and reimagine Black contributions to textile history, specifically West Africa&amp;rsquo;s ties to practices like tie-dying, sewing, embroidery, and quilting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&amp;rsquo;ll hear from the artist herself, and &lt;a href="https://english.cornell.edu/chelsea-mikael-frazier"&gt;Dr. Chelsea Frazier&lt;/a&gt;, a scholar specializing in the intersection of Black feminist literature and theory, in a special Artist Talk about how Eregbu&amp;#39;s textile and sound installation engages Black history, heritage, and diasporic memory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&amp;rsquo;t miss this chance to explore &lt;em&gt;Blue Magic &lt;/em&gt;and the enduring histories that bring this art to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Legacy of New York&lt;/strong&gt; series invites students to explore the social movements, histories, and communities that have shaped New York City. Through museum visits, walking tours, and site-based learning experiences, this series seeks to highlight and celebrate the most diverse communities, cultures, and events in the nation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
