&lt;p&gt;With alcohol being omnipresent in many networking opportunities and professional settings, this workshop aims to increase understanding of the effects of alcohol on the body, discuss protective behaviors to utilize while drinking, and walk through ways to be an active bystander in situations where alcohol is present. Participants will discuss factors that impact their choices around alcohol usage and how to navigate difficult situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Session&amp;nbsp;open&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;all&amp;nbsp;Columbia&amp;nbsp;University&amp;nbsp;students,&amp;nbsp;regardless&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;school&amp;nbsp;affiliation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Note: This session will not be recorded, and slides are not shared. If you&amp;#39;re no longer able to attend, please remove your registration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This seminar (designed in collaboration with PerLA &amp;ndash; Performance Epistemologies Research Lab, IUAV University of Venice) looks at genealogies of performance pedagogies and perspectives in blue dramaturgy. The talks will touch on interdisciplinary pedagogies and the emerging current of studies of &amp;ldquo;blue humanities&amp;rdquo; which engages with complex questions surrounding ocean and sea imaginaries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Opening Remarks:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Barbara Faedda&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;(Executive Director, Italian Academy)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
